        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ख़ज़ाना",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ख़ज़ाना — khazānā — \"a treasure; a treasury\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कहानी में राजा का ख़ज़ाना एक पुराने क़िले में था। kahānī meṁ rājā kā khazānā ek purāne qile meṁ thā. In the story the king's treasure was in an old fort."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ख़ज़ाना (khazānā) is usually traced, through Persian, to Arabic khizāna, \"a storehouse\". It is a king's treasury and, in stories, gold hidden underground."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
